# DRIFT STUDIO — THE MASTER BUILD PROMPT
## Open-AI Social Content Studio | Hacktoberfest 2026 — Week 3: Slow and Steady

You are an elite digital product studio operating as one team: an award-winning creative director, senior UI/UX designer, motion designer, frontend architect, AI engineer, and accessibility specialist.

Your mission is to design and build **Drift Studio**, a visually extraordinary, fully functional social content creation workspace powered by open-weight AI.

The visual reference is the video walkthrough supplied with this task. Study its aesthetic and interaction style carefully. Reproduce the same level of visual confidence, creative energy, editorial typography, vivid colors, graphic composition, and thoughtful scroll-based storytelling while creating an entirely original brand and interface.

Reference design:
https://dribbble.com/shots/26366091-Landing-page-design-for-a-social-media-management-platform

This is a separate project for the Hacktoberfest Open-Source AI Challenge, Week 3: "Slow and Steady".

It must NOT be a food application, meal planner, recipe generator, or recreation of SlothPlate. Give it an entirely different product purpose, information architecture, identity, and user journey.

Do not just describe what you would build. Inspect the existing workspace, then implement the actual application, test it, and refine it.

# 01. THE PRODUCT IDEA

## Brand: Drift Studio

Main tagline: "Your ideas. Already in motion."

Alternative hero statement: "Less posting. More creating."

Product description:

Drift Studio transforms one rough idea into an organized collection of platform-specific social media drafts. It uses open-weight AI to handle the repetitive work of planning posts, adapting content, drafting captions, and organizing a weekly content calendar.

The audience includes:
- Indie hackers and developers.
- Students building their personal brands.
- Freelancers and creators.
- Small businesses.
- Community managers.
- Anyone who wants to share their work without spending hours planning content.

The central promise is simple:

**Think of the idea once. Let Drift take care of the busywork.**

The entire experience should revolve around a real workflow:

1. The user enters a campaign idea.
2. They select their audience, tone, objective, and platforms.
3. An open-weight model generates relevant content variations.
4. The user edits and organizes the drafts.
5. The content moves into a weekly board or calendar.
6. The user copies or exports the finished content.

This is not another generic chatbot. It is a visual content studio with genuine AI functionality.

Do not implement fake social-media publishing. Generated content must be editable and exportable, and scheduling must be presented as a local planning feature unless a real publishing integration exists.

